From df28a12dbb3599144733e6e3a140b391fa9aa116 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:21:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: receive A-MPDUs of up to 32 KiB

b43 limits received A-MPDUs to 8 KiB, so a station sends only a few
MPDUs per PPDU, and the preamble, the block ack and the contention
around them take a large part of the airtime.

The N-PHY firmware takes the longest PSDU it receives from M_MIMO_MAXSYM
in shared memory, which brcmsmac sets to 32 KiB for every factor below
64 KiB. Firmware 666.2 has it at the same offset, and its initial
values already set it to 32 KiB. Advertise that length.

Tested on an ASUS RT-N16 as an access point with an Intel 3168 client
on channel 11, with the short guard interval: TCP from the client to
the router goes from 19-20 to 23-24 Mbit/s. 16 KiB gives the same, and
64 KiB, with M_MIMO_MAXSYM and M_WATCHDOG_8TU raised as brcmsmac does,
gives nothing more.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -374,7 +374,7 @@ static struct ieee80211_supported_band b
 	.ht_supported	= true,						\
 	.cap		= IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SM_PS |			\
 			  IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SGI_20,			\
-	.ampdu_factor	= IEEE80211_HT_MAX_AMPDU_8K,			\
+	.ampdu_factor	= IEEE80211_HT_MAX_AMPDU_32K,			\
 	.ampdu_density	= IEEE80211_HT_MPDU_DENSITY_8,			\
 	.mcs = {							\
 		.rx_mask	= { 0xff },				\
